@inherits UiComponentBase

@* A text box that filters a list, and posts the value that was chosen.

   The important part is the last clause. A combobox that only holds its value in JavaScript is
   useless to a form that posts, so underneath this is a real <input type="hidden"> carrying the
   value and a real <input type="text"> carrying what was typed. Nothing is stored anywhere else,
   which is also why a fragment swap cannot lose the selection.

   With scripting off it degrades to that text box and a visible list of options — worse than the
   filtered version, but it still submits. Where the list is a catalogue rather than a menu, put
   `up-autosubmit` and `up-target` on the input and let the server filter instead; the markup is
   otherwise the same. *@

<div data-slot="combobox" data-target="@Target" data-multiple="@(Multiple ? "true" : null)"
     class="@Cn("relative", Class)" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">@ChildContent</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The id of the <see cref="ComboboxContent"/> this opens.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Target { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>More than one value, shown as chips. The hidden inputs repeat the same name.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Multiple { get; set; }
}
